post-it: Replace the hard drive
cause: Hard drive the customer wants replaced
symptoms:
	Wants the hard drive replaced
checks:
	yes: Windows starts
	yes: Memory test passes
	yes: Windows stays up after the desktop appears
	no: Bluescreen after the desktop appears
	no: Freezes with a buzz after the desktop appears
	no: Stops at "Non-System disk or disk error"
	yes: CPU fan is clean and spins freely
	yes: Every part sits in its own place
hardware steps:
	Open case
	Take out the old hard drive
	Fit a new hard drive
	Close case
	Switch it on and check that Windows starts
notes:
	PLACEHOLDER text (#337) for the writers: the post-it, cause, symptom and steps.
	Nothing is wrong with the drive. The top hat man wants it gone because it holds evidence of his economic crimes (story/computers/0602_top_hat_man.setup). The job is fixed once a new drive is in; the old one can go in the trash or stay on the mat.
